Studio Ghibli Film Analysis
Overview
This project explores financial trends, director influence, genre distribution, and quiz generation based on a dataset of Studio Ghibli films. It uses Python and libraries like Pandas and Matplotlib to uncover insights about film profitability, genre popularity, and temporal trends.

Features
Top Films by ROI: Identifies the most profitable Ghibli films by return on investment.

Revenue Trends Over Time: Tracks total studio revenue year by year.

Budget vs. Revenue Scatterplot: Visualizes the relationship between film budgets and earnings, color-coded by director.

Miyazaki-Only Revenue Line Graph: Focuses on how Hayao Miyazaki's films have performed financially over time.

Genre Frequency & Performance:

Pie chart of genre frequency across all films

Bar chart of average revenue by primary genre

Ghibli Quiz Game: A simple Python terminal game that asks fun trivia questions based on the data.

Dataset Columns
Name: Film title

Year: Release year

Director: Film director

Screenplay: Screenwriter

Budget: Production cost (USD)

Revenue: Box office earnings (USD)

Genre 1-3: Up to 3 genre tags per film

Duration: Runtime (e.g., "1h 30m")

